        "content": "{\n  \"module\": \"pages\",\n  \"verdict\": \"needs_changes\",\n  \"tool_calls\": 49,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"packages/excalidraw/tests/pages.test.tsx\",\n      \"line\": 611,\n      \"issue\": \"In the test \\\"restores legacy single-page scenes, serializes all pages to JSON, and scopes visual exports via exportScene to the active page\\\" (lines 611-638), spying on `clipboardModule.copyTextToSystemClipboard` does not intercept `exportToClipboard({ type: \\\"json\\\", ... })` because `exportToClipboard` calls `clipboardModule.copyToClipboard`, which in turn invokes `copyTextToSystemClipboard` via a direct intra-module reference inside `clipboard.ts`, causing `copyTextToSystemClipboard` to run unmocked in jsdom and fail with `Error copying to clipboard`.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Spy on `vi.spyOn(clipboardModule, \\\"copyToClipboard\\\").mockResolvedValue()` instead of `copyTextToSystemClipboard`, and assert directly on the first argument passed to `copyToClipboard` (`expect(copySpy.mock.lastCall![0].map((el) => el.id)).toEqual([\\\"rect-p2\\\"])`).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"refinement_packets\": []\n}"
      },
